## [ENT-005] | 2026-11-17 00:06 UTC | Mercury | note | ref: game/routes/guidebook/trade.md | see: orders.log ENT-019
Goods moved and where things stand for the circuit boards (orders P5).
- @Apollo: 75 silicon ore bought at Central Nexus (420 cr plus 1% tax, 31,814 cr, booked as station stock) and deposited into the storage there of the hauler that crafts the boards; that storage read 107 silicon ore and 36 carbon ore at 2026-11-17 00:01 UTC (view of its storage). 107 silicon make 159 boards by carbon_arc_circuit_etching and take 636 carbon ore; Logistics storages at Central Nexus hold about 450 carbon there (storage book 23:38 UTC), and the station asks carbon at 4 cr in depth at Node Beta, Node Gamma and Node Alpha. The Central Nexus silicon ask left about 340 units at 420 cr after my buy (it read 425 at 23:33 UTC).
- @Zero @Apophis @Oracle: neural soma stands at 376 to 412 cr in five station bids of 5 to 15 units (books of 23:04 to 23:32 UTC) while Central Nexus offers it at 323 in depth; the fleet stores 622 soma. Five sell routes with a floor of 370 cr opened at 23:44 UTC; the first five runs sold into four bids for +321 to +1,828 cr each (data/routes/runs.jsonl), then the bids were taken. Put sell-soma-at-node-beta and sell-soma-at-synchrony into your plan's First list if your ships store soma there: they send only a pilot with its own soma in storage and a bid at the floor.
- A standing sell order costs 1% of the listed value at once (one anchor beacon listed at 1,200 cr at Node Beta: fee 12 cr, 2026-11-16 23:48 UTC); whether and when it fills is read next turn.

